<urn:atm:triage:finding/AG13-FIND-B6-LOOPBACK-RELABELED-SELFIP>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AG13-FIND-B6-LOOPBACK-RELABELED-SELFIP" ;
  triage:title "Self-IP tests remain loopback-relabeled, not proof against a real advertised interface IP" ;
  triage:description "The two self-IP test functions in crates/atm-daemon/src/tests/runtime_root/loopback.rs (post-split location; original runtime_root.rs was split by commit 714b1c67 into dispatch.rs, local_ipc.rs, loopback.rs, mod.rs) -- dispatcher_self_ip_send_rejects_disabled_host_before_mailbox_mutation (line 480, body calls RemoteTargetHost::parse(\"127.0.0.1\") at line 549) and dispatcher_secure_self_ip_requires_ack_round_trips_and_updates_reply_state (line 590, body calls the same at line 646) -- still bind/allow-list 127.0.0.1/Ipv4Addr::LOCALHOST, byte-for-byte the same mechanism as AG.12's loopback tests. AG13-QA-2 additionally confirmed via RBP that both are structurally near-identical copies of the file's pre-existing loopback test dispatcher_loopback_send_round_trips_through_peer_listener_into_self_inbox (lines 1-93) -- same tempdir/roster/allow_host('127.0.0.1', ...) scaffolding, just renamed. No fixture in the entire diff exercises the host's actual advertised/bound network-interface IP as sprint-AG13.md and the smoke checklist require." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-17T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B6/dispatcher-self-ip-send/480> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B6/dispatcher-self-ip-send/549> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B6/dispatcher-secure-self-ip/590> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B6/dispatcher-secure-self-ip/646> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG13-FIND-B6/loopback-template/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s13-selfip-proof/6d2afb4c> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s13-selfip-proof/6d2afb4c> ;
  triage:notes "Sprint AG.13 core, still-unresolved defect: tests must bind/parse against the host's actual advertised/bound network-interface IP, not 127.0.0.1/localhost, to satisfy the sprint's named deliverable 'Self-IP proof'. Two test functions (dispatcher_self_ip_send_rejects_disabled_host_before_mailbox_mutation and dispatcher_secure_self_ip_requires_ack_round_trips_and_updates_reply_state) are currently scaffolded with loopback-only fixtures identical to pre-existing loopback tests. No fixture exercises real interface IP. Structural duplication confirmed by RBP review." .

